  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cocosamide B may interact with hepatocytes through a series of molecular pathways. Specifically, Cocosamide B is predicted to target VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Oxytroflavoside B and Tubotaiwine, both of which are also predicted to target hepatocytes. This indicates a potential indirect pathway where Cocosamide B could influence hepatocyte function through VMRC-LCP. Similarly, Cocosamide B is also predicted to target MOVP-3, which is a target of Tubotaiwine, further supporting a chain of interactions leading to hepatocyte effects. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with Cocosamide B being consistently linked to a pathway that ultimately affects hepatocytes. The evidence highlights a possible mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways through these intermediaries, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
